 be deterministic, hybrid, review-based, or absent only when\nthe absence is typed as residue with owner and effect. The amendment is not\ncomplete if the changed shape can govern downstream work but has no declared\nenforcement or residue path.","excerpt_sha256":"c3a7857171cdbc15a06080706f4a60868220b91c19b17b8b7fba57c6820b89a0","necessary_declaration_guard_in_T":true,"query_id":"Change-not-ActualEnforcement","selected_in_T":false,"selector":"/voices/scientific_formal/formal_expression","source":{"definition_id":"cal.definition.schema-evolution-invariant","path":"evidence/migrations/cyberalchemy-v2-to-lab/candidates/0004-artifact-reconstruction-pipeline/layers/l1-semantic-repeatability/definitions/schema-evolution-invariant/v1/definition.json","sha256":"e1c996eda39fa109bc0b689570ce1a6cdeb72796e667125a365679ad4da26088","version_ref":"cal.definition.schema-evolution-invariant@1.0.0-candidate.1"},"start_character":0},{"actual_outcome_target_in_T":false,"clause_id":"SEI-013","end_character":415,"excerpt":"For an authority-affecting shape change `s -> s'`, a valid amendment is:\n\n```text\nA = (owner, scope, source, delta, compatibility, witness, residue)\n```\n\nwhere `witness` may be deterministic, hybrid, review-based, or absent only when\nthe absence is typed as residue with owner and effect. The amendment is not\ncomplete if the changed shape can govern downstream work but has no declared\nenforcement or residue path.","excerpt_sha256":"c3a7857171cdbc15a06080706f4a60868220b91c19b17b8b7fba57c6820b89a0","necessary_declaration_guard_in_T":true,"query_id":"Change-not-ActualWitnessAdequacy","selected_in_T":false,"selector":"/voices/scientific_formal/formal_expression","source":{"definition_id":"cal.definition.schema-evolution-invariant","path":"evidence/migrations/cyberalchemy-v2-to-lab/candidates/0004-artifact-reconstruction-pipeline/layers/l1-semantic-repeatability/definitions/schema-evolution-invariant/v1/definition.json","sha256":"e1c996eda39fa109bc0b689570ce1a6cdeb72796e667125a365679ad4da26088","version_ref":"cal.definition.schema-evolution-invariant@1.0.0-candidate.1"},"start_character":0},{"actual_outcome_target_in_T":false,"clause_id":"SEI-013","end_character":415,"excerpt":"For an authority-affecting shape change `s -> s'`, a valid amendment is:\n\n```text\nA = (owner, scope, source, delta, compatibility, witness, residue)\n```\n\nwhere `witness` may be deterministic, hybrid, review-based, or absent only when\nthe absence is typed as residue with owner and effect. The amendment is not\ncomplete if the changed shape can govern downstream work but has no declared\nenforcement or residue path.","excerpt_sha256":"c3a7857171cdbc15a06080706f4a60868220b91c19b17b8b7fba57c6820b89a0","necessary_declaration_guard_in_T":true,"query_id":"Change-not-ActualAuthority","selected_in_T":false,"selector":"/voices/scientific_formal/formal_expression","source":{"definition_id":"cal.definition.schema-evolution-invariant","path":"evidence/migrations/cyberalchemy-v2-to-lab/candidates/0004-artifact-reconstruction-pipeline/layers/l1-semantic-repeatability/definitions/schema-evolution-invariant/v1/definition.json","sha256":"e1c996eda39fa109bc0b689570ce1a6cdeb72796e667125a365679ad4da26088","version_ref":"cal.definition.schema-evolution-invariant@1.0.0-candidate.1"},"start_character":0},{"actual_outcome_target_in_T":false,"clause_id":"SEI-014","end_character":880,"excerpt":"Schema Evolution Invariant is the normalized invariant identified by semantic.schema-evolution-invariant, owned within scope.shared-authority, and carried by type.invariant. Any canonical instance must preserve that classification and the accepted source relations to CAV2-D25 without silently merging it with another target.\n\nBound source-semantic basis:\n\nSchema amendment witness is the CyberAlchemy v2 rule that any schema,\nfrontmatter, taxonomy, ontology, ledger, event, or machine-view change that\naffects validation or authority interpretation must carry both:\n\n- an amendment record naming owner, scope, reason, changed shape, source\n  evidence, compatibility effect, and rollout or rollback route\n- a witness naming the validator, runtime observation, fixture, review check,\n  or typed residue that shows how the changed rule is enforced or why it cannot\n  yet be enforced","excerpt_sha256":"f94a9d6cdebe49d62e97a63efdde1de1ab707fb1850f38e184cdfc4ff1ff3934","necessary_declaration_guard_in_T":true,"query_id":"Change-not-ActualEnforcement","selected_in_T":false,"selector":"/voices/scientific_formal/normative_statement","source":{"definition_id":"cal.definition.schema-evolution-invariant","path":"evidence/migrations/cyberalchemy-v2-to-lab/candidates/0004-artifact-reconstruction-pipeline/layers/l1-semantic-repeatability/definitions/schema-evolution-invariant/v1/definition.json","sha256":"e1c996eda39fa109bc0b689570ce1a6cdeb72796e667125a365679ad4da26088","version_ref":"cal.definition.schema-evolution-invariant@1.0.0-candidate.1"},"start_character":0},{"actual_outcome_target_in_T":false,"clause_id":"SEI-014","end_character":880,"excerpt":"Schema Evolution Invariant is the normalized invariant identified by semantic.schema-evolution-invariant, owned within scope.shared-authority, and carried by type.invariant. Any canonical instance must preserve that classification and the accepted source relations to CAV2-D25 without silently merging it with another target.\n\nBound source-semantic basis:\n\nSchema amendment witness is the CyberAlchemy v2 rule that any schema,\nfrontmatter, taxonomy, ontology, ledger, event, or machine-view change that\naffects validation or authority interpretation must carry both:\n\n- an amendment record naming owner, scope, reason, changed shape, source\n  evidence, compatibility effect, and rollout or rollback route\n- a witness naming the validator, runtime observation, fixture, review check,\n  or typed residue that shows how the changed rule is enforced or why it cannot\n  yet be enforced","excerpt_sha256":"f94a9d6cdeb